"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MaximalCliques"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Every maximal clique of an undirected graph’s simple graph once, lazily, each in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order (by vertex index): an isolated vertex, or one whose only edges are loops, is a clique of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one. The order is Eppstein–Löffler–Strash’s: by the cliques’ first vertex in"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"coreNumbers().degeneracyOrdering","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", then as Bron–Kerbosch with Tomita’s pivot (ties to the least","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"index) and branches in ascending index meets them. The sequence holds the graph, so iterating","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"again gives the same cliques. O(n + m) before the first clique, O(d·n·3^(d\/3)) in all for","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"degeneracy d."}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/MaximalCliques/lazy":{"title":"lazy","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/maximalcliques\/lazy","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques\/lazy","abstract":[],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"lazy"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s12LazySequenceV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"LazySequence"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques":{"title":"Cliques","url":"\/documentation\/cliques","abstract":[],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques","role":"collection","kind":"symbol"}}}